algorithms.pseudocode:
function TrialDivisionBounded(N):
    for d = 2 to ⌊√N⌋:
        if d | N: return d
    return 'prime'

Correctness: By composite_iff_exists_divisor_le_sqrt
Complexity: O(√N) time, O(1) space

function SieveCertified(limit):
    is_prime[0..limit] ← all true
    is_prime[0], is_prime[1] ← false
    for p = 2 to ⌊√limit⌋:  // certified complete
        if is_prime[p]:
            mark p², p²+p, ... as composite
    return {i : is_prime[i]}

Correctness: composite_detection_complete_on_Icc
Complexity: O(n log log n)
